<title>CHINA: China January sugar output up 19.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>China January sugar output up 19.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>China produced 1.7138 million tonnes of sugar in January, up 19.4 percent compared with the year-earlier period, the State Statistical Bureau said on Thursday.</p>
<p>China produced 8.4 million tonnes of sugar in 1996, up 13.15 percent from 1995, the bureau has said.</p>
<p>China's sugar crushing season lasts from October to April.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532 1921</p>
